# Security and RBAC

## Authorization
- Server is authoritative. Hiding a button is cosmetic.
- Every controller action authorizes before it does work. In Ticketing, E-Forms, DocExtract and Document Control that is `abort_unless($request->user()?->can('...'), 403)` on the controller. No route without auth middleware unless explicitly public and commented.
- Permissions (Spatie Permission 7): name them `<module>:<resource>:<action>`, matching the existing strings (`ticketing:tickets:create`, `e_approval:forms:manage`, `doc-extract:run`, `documents:controlled:view`). Code checks permissions, never role names. The sole workspace-owner role is `tenant_admin` (full enabled permission set, empty entity matrix). Do not treat ATC `admin` or leftover `administrator` as the owner; hide `administrator` from Team & Access and fold assignments onto `tenant_admin`. `dynamic_entities_admin` is the scoped Dynamic Entities module admin.
- Sensitive actions (delete, approve, export, role change, billing change) need explicit permissions and an audit entry.
- Frontend: use the existing helpers in `frontend/lib/rbac`. Do not add a second permission-check mechanism.

## Authentication
- Sanctum for the first-party SPA/app. Passport only for third-party OAuth2 clients and machine-to-machine APIs. Do not mix them on one route group.
- MFA and passkeys (WebAuthn) live in the Identity module. Never bypass, weaken or special-case them. Enforce SSO for tenants that enable it.
- Rate-limit login, MFA, password reset, token and export endpoints.

## Input, output, transport
- Validate everything server-side, whitelist fields, and return only the fields the service payload includes.
- Strict CORS, CSP, HSTS, secure cookies.
- Uploads (Documents, DocExtract, e-approval imports): size and type limits, content sniffing, virus-scan hook, never served from a public path.
- Tenant-configurable outbound URLs (webhooks, Teams, callbacks): require HTTPS, block private/link-local/loopback IPs and redirects to them (SSRF), set short timeouts, sign payloads. Test-email and test-webhook endpoints are rate-limited and permission-gated.
- Secrets never in the repo, logs or client bundles. Only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are public.
- Run `composer audit` and `npm audit` in CI. PII: minimize, encrypt sensitive columns, redact in logs.
